# The keys that may sign a release tag (decision 0041). The release job reads
# this file from main, never from the tag, and builds only from an annotated
# tag that one of these keys signed (scripts/verify-tag.sh).
#
# One line for each maintainer's key, in the allowed signers format of
# ssh-keygen, with the namespace "git":
#   <email> namespaces="git" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA... <comment>
# Each key is a hardware key (sk-ssh-ed25519 or sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256), and
# the gate refuses any other line that is not a comment. A new key reaches
# this file only through a pull request to main. docs/contributing/releasing.md
# says how to make one.
#
# Check a tag by hand, before you push it:
#   git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=.github/tag-signers verify-tag vX.Y.Z
#
# No key is listed yet. Until the owner adds the line of their hardware key,
# the release job refuses every tag.
